---
const tarjetas = [
  ["Docs drift silently", "Nothing fails when code and docs disagree. The page just keeps saying the wrong thing."],
  ["Review doesn't catch it", "A pull request that changes a function rarely touches the page that explains it."],
  ["Checkers are hosted and paid", "Tools that tie docs to code usually live in someone's cloud. DocKeeper runs on your machine, for free."],
];
---
<section id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
    <h2>Writing docs is free now. Keeping them true isn't.</h2>
    <p class="lead">An agent can write a README in seconds. Three months later it describes functions that were renamed, flags that were removed and flows that changed, and nobody knows which pages are lying.</p>
    <div class="cards3">
      {tarjetas.map(([titulo, texto]) => <div class="card"><h3>{titulo}</h3><p>{texto}</p></div>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
